  "solution": {
    "approach": "Check Odd or Even without using arithmetic operators by testing least significant bit (n & 1).",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) == 1) {\n        if ((n & 1) == 0) printf(\"Even\\n\");\n        else printf(\"Odd\\n\");\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (cin >> n) {\n        if ((n & 1) == 0) cout << \"Even\\n\";\n        else cout << \"Odd\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int n = sc.nextInt();\n            System.out.println((n & 1) == 0 ? \"Even\" : \"Odd\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        n = int(s)\n        print(\"Even\" if (n & 1) == 0 else \"Odd\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\n    if (s.length > 0) {\n        const n = parseInt(s, 10);\n        console.log((n & 1) === 0 ? \"Even\" : \"Odd\");\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Bitwise AND with 1 tests the parity: if (n & 1) == 0 then Even, else Odd."
  },
  "hints": [
    "Arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /, %) are forbidden.",
    "Use bitwise AND '&' with 1.",
    "If (n & 1) == 0, the last bit is 0, so number is Even."
  ],
